   CCrreeaattee aanndd uussee aann AARRMMvv77 cchhrroooott oonn aann AAMMDD6644 hhoosstt
     Use an existing source tree to build a chroot host with architecture
     overrides:

          D=/path/to/chroot
          cd /usr/src
          mkdir -p $D
          make world TARGET=arm TARGET_ARCH=armv7 DESTDIR=$D
          make distribution TARGET=arm TARGET_ARCH=armv7 DESTDIR=$D

     With _e_m_u_l_a_t_o_r_s_/_q_e_m_u_-_u_s_e_r_-_s_t_a_t_i_c from the FreeBSD Ports Collection, the
     emulator must be copied into the jail path specified in the bbiinnmmiissccccttll
     command.  Using the example above:

           mkdir $D/usr/local/bin
           cp /usr/local/bin/qemu-arm-static $D/usr/local/bin

     Now the user can chroot into the environment normally, as root:

           chroot $D

